WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 2: Good Neighbours and Jobs.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.820
In this unit you meet the people who live and work in
your neighbourhood, and you find out what their jobs are.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.140
You learn twenty-one words for helpers, for their special
clothes and equipment, and for the actions they do,

4
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.440
from the window cleaner and the bus driver
to the firefighter, the nurse and the farmer.

5
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:25.060
You learn to ask questions with What
and Who, to count people and objects,

6
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:30.890
and to say what somebody is doing right now
with is or are and a verb ending in -ing.

7
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:36.240
By the end you can describe a job, name
the equipment that keeps a worker safe,

8
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.480
and be a good neighbour like the children in
this unit's story, The Helpers of Warta Street.

9
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.880
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.510
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name the
different people who live and work in your neighbourhood.

11
00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.360
You will also describe a job and
explain what the person does in it.

12
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.280
You will also ask and answer questions using What and Who.

13
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.800
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:10.280
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: day, stay, tray, key, need, farmer.

15
00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.340
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

16
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:23.190
The reading sequence includes Firefighters and
Their Equipment and A Poem: “My Neighbourhood”.

17
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.760
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

18
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.760
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

19
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.940
The first language focus is What
and Who: Choosing the Question Word.

20
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.840
We use question words to ask for information.

21
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.900
What asks about a thing, an action or a job.

22
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.680
Who asks about a person.

23
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.540
These two little words help you find out
about the helpers in your neighbourhood.

24
00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.260
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

25
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.700
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Describe a Job.

26
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.880
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

27
00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:08.400
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

28
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.300
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:16.580
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

30
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:23.500
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
